{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000200",
  "title": "Sine/Cosine Phase Explorer",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": "[profile.release]\nopt-level = 1\nlto = false\ncodegen-units = 16",
  "description": "Interactively explore phase shifts applied to sine and cosine waves. Use the slider to shift the phase φ and watch the waves respond in real time via LiveView SVG rendering.",
  "tags": [
    "math",
    "interactive",
    "visualization",
    "trigonometry",
    "liveview"
  ],
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "# Sine/Cosine Phase Explorer 🌊\n\nSinusoidal functions are the building blocks of wave phenomena in physics, signal processing, and mathematics. This notebook lets you **interactively explore phase shifts** applied to sine and cosine waves.\n\n## The Functions\n\n$$y = \\sin(x + \\varphi) \\qquad y = \\cos(x + \\varphi)$$\n\nwhere $\\varphi$ (phi) is the **phase shift** — how much the wave is displaced horizontally.\n\n## Key Identity\n\n$$\\cos(x) = \\sin\\!\\left(x + \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$$\n\nCosine is just sine shifted left by $\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}$ radians (90°). In this explorer, watch how the two waves maintain that exact $\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}$ separation as you change the phase.\n\n## What Phase Shift Means Geometrically\n\nA phase shift $\\varphi$ **translates the wave horizontally** by $\\varphi$ units to the left:\n\n- $\\varphi = 0$ → standard sine/cosine positions\n- $\\varphi = \\pi/2$ → sine looks like cosine; cosine looks like $-\\sin$\n- $\\varphi = \\pi$ → both waves are inverted (sin → −sin, cos → −cos)\n- $\\varphi = 2\\pi$ → full cycle; waves return to original position\n\nUse the **Phase Shift slider** in the next cell to explore these transformations in real time!",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Phase Control",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "ui::slider(\"phase\", 0.0, 6.2832)\n    .step(0.01)\n    .label(\"Phase Shift (φ)\")\n    .default_value(0.0)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Phase Visualization",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use ironpad_cell::prelude::*;\n\nstruct PhaseExplorer;\n\nimpl LiveView for PhaseExplorer {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        Self\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> LiveContent {\n        let phase = sim::read::<f64>(\"phase\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n\n        let w: f64 = 780.0;\n        let h: f64 = 390.0;\n        let ml: f64 = 60.0;\n        let mr: f64 = 20.0;\n        let mt: f64 = 38.0;\n        let mb: f64 = 48.0;\n        let pw = w - ml - mr;\n        let ph = h - mt - mb;\n        let pi = std::f64::consts::PI;\n        let x_max = 4.0 * pi;\n        let y_min = -1.2_f64;\n        let y_max = 1.2_f64;\n\n        let x_to_px = |x: f64| ml + x / x_max * pw;\n        let y_to_px = |y: f64| mt + (y_max - y) / (y_max - y_min) * ph;\n\n        // Build polyline points (400 segments for smooth curves)\n        let n: usize = 400;\n        let mut sin_pts = String::with_capacity(n * 14);\n        let mut cos_pts = String::with_capacity(n * 14);\n        for i in 0..=n {\n            let x = i as f64 / n as f64 * x_max;\n            let px = x_to_px(x);\n            let sy = y_to_px((x + phase).sin());\n            let cy = y_to_px((x + phase).cos());\n            if !sin_pts.is_empty() {\n                sin_pts.push(' ');\n                cos_pts.push(' ');\n            }\n            sin_pts.push_str(&format!(\"{px:.1},{sy:.1}\"));\n            cos_pts.push_str(&format!(\"{px:.1},{cy:.1}\"));\n        }\n\n        // Vertical grid lines at multiples of π/2\n        let grid_x_defs: &[(f64, &str)] = &[\n            (0.5 * pi, \"\\u{03c0}/2\"),\n            (pi, \"\\u{03c0}\"),\n            (1.5 * pi, \"3\\u{03c0}/2\"),\n            (2.0 * pi, \"2\\u{03c0}\"),\n            (2.5 * pi, \"5\\u{03c0}/2\"),\n            (3.0 * pi, \"3\\u{03c0}\"),\n            (3.5 * pi, \"7\\u{03c0}/2\"),\n            (4.0 * pi, \"4\\u{03c0}\"),\n        ];\n\n        let bot = mt + ph;\n        let right = ml + pw;\n\n        let mut vgrid = String::new();\n        let mut x_labels = String::new();\n        for (xv, lbl) in grid_x_defs {\n            let px = x_to_px(*xv);\n            vgrid.push_str(&format!(\n                \"<line x1=\\\"{px:.1}\\\" y1=\\\"{mt:.1}\\\" x2=\\\"{px:.1}\\\" y2=\\\"{bot:.1}\\\" stroke=\\\"#1c1c38\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\"/>\"\n            ));\n            x_labels.push_str(&format!(\n                \"<text x=\\\"{px:.1}\\\" y=\\\"{y:.1}\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" fill=\\\"#505070\\\" font-size=\\\"11\\\" font-family=\\\"monospace\\\">{lbl}</text>\",\n                y = bot + 17.0\n            ));\n        }\n\n        // Horizontal grid lines at -1, -0.5, 0, 0.5, 1\n        let mut hgrid = String::new();\n        let mut y_labels = String::new();\n        for &yv in &[-1.0_f64, -0.5, 0.0, 0.5, 1.0] {\n            let py = y_to_px(yv);\n            hgrid.push_str(&format!(\n                \"<line x1=\\\"{ml:.1}\\\" y1=\\\"{py:.1}\\\" x2=\\\"{right:.1}\\\" y2=\\\"{py:.1}\\\" stroke=\\\"#1c1c38\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\"/>\"\n            ));\n            y_labels.push_str(&format!(\n                \"<text x=\\\"{x:.1}\\\" y=\\\"{py:.1}\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" dominant-baseline=\\\"middle\\\" fill=\\\"#505070\\\" font-size=\\\"11\\\" font-family=\\\"monospace\\\">{yv:.1}</text>\",\n                x = ml - 5.0\n            ));\n        }\n\n        // Phase indicator — vertical dashed line at x = phase (mod 4π)\n        let phase_x = x_to_px(phase % x_max);\n        let axis_y = y_to_px(0.0);\n\n        // Phase value display\n        let phase_turns = phase / (2.0 * pi);\n        let phase_deg = phase * 180.0 / pi;\n        let phase_info = format!(\n            \"\\u{03c6} = {:.4} rad = {:.1}\\u{00b0} = {:.4}\\u{03c4}\",\n            phase, phase_deg, phase_turns\n        );\n\n        // Legend box position (top-right inside plot)\n        let lx = right - 196.0;\n        let l1x = lx + 10.0;\n        let l1xe = lx + 44.0;\n        let ltx = lx + 50.0;\n\n        let svg = format!(\n            \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" width=\\\"{w}\\\" height=\\\"{h}\\\" style=\\\"display:block;border-radius:10px;\\\">\\\n<defs>\\\n<linearGradient id=\\\"ipbg\\\" x1=\\\"0\\\" y1=\\\"0\\\" x2=\\\"0\\\" y2=\\\"1\\\">\\\n<stop offset=\\\"0%\\\" stop-color=\\\"#08081a\\\"/>\\\n<stop offset=\\\"100%\\\" stop-color=\\\"#0e0e24\\\"/>\\\n</linearGradient>\\\n<filter id=\\\"glow\\\">\\\n<feGaussianBlur stdDeviation=\\\"2\\\" result=\\\"blur\\\"/>\\\n<feMerge><feMergeNode in=\\\"blur\\\"/><feMergeNode in=\\\"SourceGraphic\\\"/></feMerge>\\\n</filter>\\\n</defs>\\\n<rect width=\\\"{w}\\\" height=\\\"{h}\\\" fill=\\\"url(#ipbg)\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\"/>\\\n{vgrid}{hgrid}\\\n<line x1=\\\"{ml:.1}\\\" y1=\\\"{axis_y:.1}\\\" x2=\\\"{right:.1}\\\" y2=\\\"{axis_y:.1}\\\" stroke=\\\"#2e2e52\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1.5\\\"/>\\\n<line x1=\\\"{ml:.1}\\\" y1=\\\"{mt:.1}\\\" x2=\\\"{ml:.1}\\\" y2=\\\"{bot:.1}\\\" stroke=\\\"#2e2e52\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1.5\\\"/>\\\n<line x1=\\\"{phase_x:.1}\\\" y1=\\\"{mt:.1}\\\" x2=\\\"{phase_x:.1}\\\" y2=\\\"{bot:.1}\\\" stroke=\\\"#ffd54f\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1.5\\\" stroke-dasharray=\\\"6,4\\\" opacity=\\\"0.8\\\"/>\\\n<polyline points=\\\"{cos_pts}\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#ff6b6b\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\" stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" filter=\\\"url(#glow)\\\"/>\\\n<polyline points=\\\"{sin_pts}\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#4fc3f7\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\" stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" filter=\\\"url(#glow)\\\"/>\\\n{x_labels}{y_labels}\\\n<rect x=\\\"{lx:.1}\\\" y=\\\"12\\\" width=\\\"192\\\" height=\\\"64\\\" rx=\\\"7\\\" fill=\\\"#08081a\\\" fill-opacity=\\\"0.92\\\" stroke=\\\"#252545\\\"/>\\\n<line x1=\\\"{l1x:.1}\\\" y1=\\\"34\\\" x2=\\\"{l1xe:.1}\\\" y2=\\\"34\\\" stroke=\\\"#4fc3f7\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"/>\\\n<text x=\\\"{ltx:.1}\\\" y=\\\"38\\\" fill=\\\"#c0c0e0\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"monospace\\\">sin(x + \\u03c6)</text>\\\n<line x1=\\\"{l1x:.1}\\\" y1=\\\"57\\\" x2=\\\"{l1xe:.1}\\\" y2=\\\"57\\\" stroke=\\\"#ff6b6b\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"/>\\\n<text x=\\\"{ltx:.1}\\\" y=\\\"61\\\" fill=\\\"#c0c0e0\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"monospace\\\">cos(x + \\u03c6)</text>\\\n<text x=\\\"{right:.1}\\\" y=\\\"{phase_y:.1}\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" fill=\\\"#ffd54f\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"monospace\\\">{phase_info}</text>\\\n</svg>\",\n            phase_y = mt - 12.0,\n        );\n\n        LiveContent::Html(svg)\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        30\n    }\n}\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    }
  ]
}
